r['interpretation']=(i[:k] if k>=0 else i)+(' Q4 (revised): the H13CN 4-3 limits (HCN/H13CN >8 at N and S, empirical-null range >4.5-16) do not measure HCN opacity (RADEX HCN/H13CN >=0.73 A even at tau>100); the N "hint" (alpha 0.03-0.075) is not a detection after control/mock tests. A joint RADEX fit of HCN and HCO+ ladders and peak ratios at S favours both lines thick with HCN sub-thermal (Tex ~6 vs ~10 K) or HCN less beam-filling (A or B, indistinguishable), and disfavours thin-HCN/abundance-only models (C, D; dchi2>=13) - this replaces the earlier "HCN thin-ish at S". HCN vs HCO+ abundance (X ratio 3-5 at S) cannot be separated from excitation. No IR pumping (v2=1f/v=0 <0.05-0.09), SO is cold (Trot <~12 K at f=1, <~25 K at 99.7% for f=0.5-1; scope 6-9" beam), CH3OH/HCO+ <0.013/<0.017 at the nuclei; CH3OH Q-branch excess is not a maser signature (neither required nor excluded). The 100-pc-scale source is resolved at 0.25" (dilution 0.8-0.9); with Tex 6-10 K the filling is ~0.5-1, not <0.1.')
